but they into selling meds too.


00:46:35.592 --> 00:46:37.082
All right, thanks.


00:46:37.127 --> 00:46:39.994
Yeah. Wait, Ana.
Hook me up.


00:46:40.030 --> 00:46:41.657
lf l find out any more about
Amare, l'll get at you.


00:46:41.698 --> 00:46:43.188
All right, l'm gonna
hold you to that.


00:46:43.233 --> 00:46:44.530
Gotcha.


00:46:44.568 --> 00:46:47.537
Don't let Sister Bernice
catch you with those.


00:46:56.046 --> 00:46:59.607
Hey, how you doing?
My name is Ana Wallace.


00:46:59.650 --> 00:47:01.743
l'm from an outreach group
called Life Support.


00:47:01.785 --> 00:47:03.013
What's wrong with your feet?


00:47:03.053 --> 00:47:04.850
Must be walking on them
too much, you know?


00:47:04.888 --> 00:47:07.880
Anyway, l'm looking for this kid
right here. His name is Amare.


00:47:07.925 --> 00:47:09.290
l thought you might know him.


00:47:11.929 --> 00:47:13.590
- He's cute.
- Mm-hmm.


00:47:13.630 --> 00:47:15.359
- Sorry.
- No?


00:47:15.399 --> 00:47:16.764
l wish l did.


00:47:16.800 --> 00:47:18.859
All right.
Well, thank you.


00:47:18.902 --> 00:47:20.631
You think you could
help me out?


00:47:22.306 --> 00:47:24.968
l need some money so me and my
boyfriend could get off these streets.


00:47:26.410 --> 00:47:28.901
Well, l don't have
no money for you,


00:47:28.946 --> 00:47:31.471
but l do work for
this HlV prevention


00:47:31.515 --> 00:47:33.278
and support program.


00:47:33.317 --> 00:47:36.775
Now, if you fit this profile,
we could definitely help you.


00:47:36.820 --> 00:47:39.755
We got free testing,
free counseling services,


00:47:39.790 --> 00:47:41.758
some condoms in the bottom
of that bag too.


00:47:41.792 --> 00:47:42.986
Okay.


00:47:43.026 --> 00:47:46.792
- What's your name?
- Andre.


00:47:46.830 --> 00:47:48.764
All right, l'm gonna
be looking for you.


00:47:48.799 --> 00:47:50.960
- Okay.
- Okay.


00:47:51.001 --> 00:47:52.298
Miss?


00:47:53.704 --> 00:47:55.672
You sure you can't
spare anything?


00:48:07.284 --> 00:48:09.684
Here. $5.
Now you got more than me.


00:48:09.720 --> 00:48:11.620
Don't spend it on no drugs, either.


00:48:11.655 --> 00:48:13.282
l don't do drugs.


00:48:14.625 --> 00:48:17.116
Okay, well...


00:48:17.160 --> 00:48:19.128
call that number, all right?


00:48:24.935 --> 00:48:27.028
- Tender?
- Mm-hmm.


00:48:27.070 --> 00:48:29.504
Describe for me how the
sensations have changed.


00:48:30.707 --> 00:48:33.733
They tingle like l got
frostbite or something.


00:48:33.777 --> 00:48:36.712
- Has the Neurotin helped with the pain?
- l stopped taking it.


00:48:36.747 --> 00:48:39.238
- Ana.
- How am l supposed to make it to work


00:48:39.283 --> 00:48:41.717
and take Kim to school?
l can't even get past the bathroom.


00:48:42.920 --> 00:48:45.388
All right.


00:48:47.591 --> 00:48:50.355
l'm gonna replace it with Vicodin.


00:48:50.394 --> 00:48:51.691
Try it. Let me know
if it works better.


00:48:51.728 --> 00:48:53.252
Great. Another drug.


00:48:55.198 --> 00:48:56.927
Look, we got to wrap this up.


00:48:56.967 --> 00:48:59.162
l got to get to my daughter's
basketball game.


00:48:59.202 --> 00:49:00.635
lf you don't slow down,


00:49:00.671 --> 00:49:04.232
you're gonna lose
the use of your feet,


00:49:04.274 --> 00:49:06.606
- period.
- Well, what you want me to do,


00:49:06.643 --> 00:49:09.339
lie in bed all day
thinking about dying?


00:49:09.379 --> 00:49:11.210
We've been through this, Ana.


00:49:11.248 --> 00:49:13.341
You got to take better
care of yourself.


00:49:13.383 --> 00:49:16.546
This virus will make you
a cripple if you let it.


00:49:21.224 --> 00:49:23.624
Thank you.


00:49:30.233 --> 00:49:31.860
Hey, Ma, you should've seen it.


00:49:31.902 --> 00:49:33.267
Kelly had 1 2 points
and a lot of assists.


00:49:33.303 --> 00:49:34.702
Yeah, you missed it.


00:49:34.738 --> 00:49:38.230
l got held up at the doctor.
l'm sorry, baby.


00:49:38.275 --> 00:49:40.971
You should've seen
her hustling all over that court.


00:49:41.011 --> 00:49:42.945
She made me so proud.
She's fierce.


00:49:42.980 --> 00:49:44.948
She's really
getting good at this.


00:49:46.650 --> 00:49:48.242
- Can l stay over with Kelly?
- Not tonight, Kim.


00:49:48.285 --> 00:49:50.845
You'll see her this weekend.


00:49:50.887 --> 00:49:53.515
- l need to talk to you about Amare.
- What about that boy?


00:49:53.557 --> 00:49:55.957
Nothing, Ma.
lt's between me and Kelly.


00:49:57.928 --> 00:49:59.395
Fine. Don't tell me, then.


00:49:59.429 --> 00:50:01.363
He's just in a little trouble.


00:50:01.398 --> 00:50:03.366
l'm just trying to get him
into a shelter, that's all.


00:50:05.235 --> 00:50:08.204
l'll wait for you in the car.
Come on. Let's go.


00:50:13.043 --> 00:50:15.068
How could you throw
a sick boy out on the streets?


00:50:15.112 --> 00:50:17.307
- That's just plain cruel.
- Grandma didn't throw him


00:50:17.347 --> 00:50:19.611
- out on the street, Ma.
- She did, last summer.


00:50:19.649 --> 00:50:22.277
He stole her pearl earrings, Ma.
You forget about that?


00:50:22.319 --> 00:50:23.877
So, what?
You giving up on him now too?


00:50:23.920 --> 00:50:25.547
- No.
- Am l out here wasting my time?


00:50:25.589 --> 00:50:27.989
'Cause my feet hurt.
l don't need to go through this.


00:50:33.196 --> 00:50:36.029
Look, that boy ain't thinking straight.


00:50:36.066 --> 00:50:39.058
He's not taking his pills.
He's selling his steroids.


00:50:39.102 --> 00:50:41.297
And being out there on the street,


00:50:41.338 --> 00:50:43.772
- l mean, that's like a death sentence.
- l know that, Ma.


00:50:43.807 --> 00:50:45.536
Did you know he was
selling his meds?


00:50:45.575 --> 00:50:48.510
Nah. l mean l knew he was in trouble.
That's why l came to you for help.


00:50:48.545 --> 00:50:51.275
All right.


00:50:51.314 --> 00:50:54.750
But what about this
boyfriend of his? Michael?


00:50:54.785 --> 00:50:56.616
l went by his studio,
remember?


00:50:56.653 --> 00:50:59.520
He acted like he
barely even knew Amare.


00:50:59.556 --> 00:51:01.922
Yo, Kelly!
Grandma's outside waiting for you!


00:51:05.462 --> 00:51:08.192
Kelly, l really am sorry
l missed your game, babe.


00:51:08.231 --> 00:51:09.960
Whatever, Ma.


00:52:02.152 --> 00:52:04.586
- Hey, come here.
- Stop it.


00:52:07.090 --> 00:52:09.354
Oh, someone told me the other day
l was supposed to use this.


00:52:09.392 --> 00:52:11.451
Put that away.


00:52:13.130 --> 00:52:15.121
- Speak of the devil.
- Ah.


00:52:16.666 --> 00:52:19.226
Yo, so how come your Mom
be passing out rubbers and shit?


00:52:19.269 --> 00:52:21.829
'Cause she works for
an AlDS outreach group.


00:52:21.872 --> 00:52:24.739
- For real?
- Yeah.


00:52:24.774 --> 00:52:27.868
Oh, that's some heavy
shit right there.


00:52:27.911 --> 00:52:31.074
l couldn't do it-- you know,
being around them people all the time.


00:52:31.114 --> 00:52:33.412
- l'd be, like, paranoid.
- Yeah.


00:52:36.586 --> 00:52:38.577
Amare?


00:52:38.622 --> 00:52:40.055
Amare, hold up!


00:52:40.090 --> 00:52:41.648
Hey wait, Kelly!
What's going on?


00:52:41.691 --> 00:52:44.216
Who is that?


00:52:46.763 --> 00:52:48.560
You okay?


00:52:59.176 --> 00:53:01.007
What do you think
you're doing?


00:53:01.044 --> 00:53:04.241
Do you know the fright you gave me when
l looked in your room and you were gone?


00:53:04.281 --> 00:53:06.476
Where have you been?


00:53:06.516 --> 00:53:08.746
And don't even think
about lying to me.


00:53:11.188 --> 00:53:12.416
l was out with Markus.


00:53:12.455 --> 00:53:13.888
Till 1 :00 in the morning?


00:53:13.924 --> 00:53:15.391
Have you lost your mind?


00:53:15.425 --> 00:53:17.916
- l'm sorry, Grandma, but--
- But nothing!


00:53:19.563 --> 00:53:22.054
l do not want you having
the same kind of life as your mother!


00:53:22.098 --> 00:53:24.396
l can't stand it!
l can't stand it!


00:53:25.869 --> 00:53:27.530
Now, you need
to be very careful


00:53:27.571 --> 00:53:29.471
about the people that
you pick for your friends


00:53:29.506 --> 00:53:31.667
and the influence that
they have on your life.


00:53:31.708 --> 00:53:34.939
You have to be very careful,
and l'm not putting up with it.


00:53:34.978 --> 00:53:37.811
And l don't want to see it again.


00:53:37.847 --> 00:53:39.474
l don't want you coming
in here this time of night.


00:53:39.516 --> 00:53:42.076
l want you coming in here
at a reasonable time.


00:53:42.118 --> 00:53:44.109
And if you can't come
in here at a reasonable time,


00:53:44.154 --> 00:53:46.122
then you don't need to go out.


00:53:46.156 --> 00:53:47.589
Or you need to go someplace else


00:53:47.624 --> 00:53:49.251
where they don't have
any rules and regulations.


00:53:51.194 --> 00:53:52.855
Grandma, it's not what you think.


00:53:52.896 --> 00:53:55.330
l saw Amare and he left before
l even had a chance to talk to him.


00:53:55.365 --> 00:53:58.129
That boy has brought
nothing but trouble


00:53:58.168 --> 00:53:59.328
into this house.


00:53:59.369 --> 00:54:01.564
Grandma, he's sick


00:54:01.605 --> 00:54:03.573
and he's gonna die
if somebody doesn't help him.


00:54:03.607 --> 00:54:05.131
You might not care
about that, but l do!


00:54:05.175 --> 00:54:07.166
Don't talk to me about
l don't care. Nuh-uh.


00:54:08.912 --> 00:54:10.846
Amare's welcome in this house


00:54:10.880 --> 00:54:12.347
as long he's willing to abide


00:54:12.382 --> 00:54:14.316
by the rules and regulations.


00:54:14.351 --> 00:54:16.819
And last summer, when
he started all of that,


00:54:16.853 --> 00:54:19.686
''Oh, the house got robbed'' stuff,


00:54:19.723 --> 00:54:22.453
l'm sorry, baby, but
that was unacceptable to me.


00:54:22.492 --> 00:54:25.222
l'm willing to help Amare


00:54:25.262 --> 00:54:27.492
when he's ready.


00:54:33.136 --> 00:54:35.001
Well, Grandma,
it's kind of crazy


00:54:35.038 --> 00:54:37.199
'cause l feel like half the time
he doesn't even want my help.


00:54:37.240 --> 00:54:39.071
He be lying and playing me,


00:54:39.109 --> 00:54:41.077
and l don't understand why
he would do something like that.


00:54:41.111 --> 00:54:43.841
Well, that's just like your mother.
She tried every trick in the book.


00:54:43.880 --> 00:54:46.849
But Ma is not like Amare.


00:54:52.522 --> 00:54:55.252
Ana hurt me.


00:54:58.762 --> 00:55:01.697
lt's taken me a long
time to forgive her.


00:55:01.731 --> 00:55:04.029
And sometimes l still can't.


00:55:06.369 --> 00:55:09.463
l try my best to remember
everything she's done with herself


00:55:09.506 --> 00:55:11.838
ever since she stopped
messing with those drugs...


00:55:14.678 --> 00:55:16.145
because she does try.


00:55:23.987 --> 00:55:25.784
Hey, Sandra.


00:55:25.822 --> 00:55:27.687
- Hey.
- How's it going?


00:55:28.692 --> 00:55:30.557
Bad day, Ana.


00:55:40.003 --> 00:55:43.234
She was just in here last week.
She was healthy as could be.


00:55:43.273 --> 00:55:45.434
lt wasn't the virus that killed her.


00:55:47.477 --> 00:55:49.707
Her husband shot her.


00:55:54.050 --> 00:55:56.143
Did you do a
domestic-violence screening?


00:55:56.186 --> 00:55:57.881
l asked her.


00:56:03.927 --> 00:56:05.292
Hey.


00:56:05.328 --> 00:56:07.922
There wasn't anything
else you could have done.


00:56:07.964 --> 00:56:09.955
l'm sorry, girl.


00:56:18.575 --> 00:56:20.338
Damn, Deyah.


00:56:21.878 --> 00:56:24.176
Why didn't you say something?


00:57:05.054 --> 00:57:06.351
Already?


00:57:06.389 --> 00:57:09.085
Mm-hmm.
Some college girl took it.


00:57:09.125 --> 00:57:11.753
The realtor said her
father's putting up cash.


00:57:12.829 --> 00:57:14.956
l know. Surprised me too.


00:57:18.935 --> 00:57:20.300
Did Kelly say what
she wanted to do yet?


00:57:20.336 --> 00:57:22.702
Ask her. Kelly!


00:57:22.739 --> 00:57:24.434
Ma, don't put me in that position.


00:57:29.379 --> 00:57:30.812
Ana wants to ask you a question.


00:57:40.089 --> 00:57:42.922
So, you watch that
Chris Tucker movie l got you?


00:57:42.959 --> 00:57:45.325
Yeah, he crazy.


00:57:45.361 --> 00:57:47.852
l thought you would like it.


00:57:52.635 --> 00:57:54.603
Why don't you come live with me


00:57:54.637 --> 00:57:57.504
when your grandma moves?


00:57:57.540 --> 00:57:58.837
But, Ma...


00:57:58.875 --> 00:58:00.900
you know l always wanted
to leave New York.


00:58:00.944 --> 00:58:04.277
And l'm going to college
down south anyway.


00:58:04.314 --> 00:58:06.009
lt'll be a good transition.


00:58:09.853 --> 00:58:11.844
So, that's it. You decided?


00:58:11.888 --> 00:58:13.981
Mm-hmm.


00:58:16.493 --> 00:58:18.393
Look, Ma, don't take it personally.


00:58:18.428 --> 00:58:20.020
l just think it would be a good idea.


00:58:20.063 --> 00:58:22.725
lt's not me l'm worried about.
lt's-- it's Kim.


00:58:25.101 --> 00:58:27.399
Maybe we should cut back
on the sleepovers,


00:58:27.437 --> 00:58:29.769
'cause she really
looks up to you


00:58:29.806 --> 00:58:33.640
and we got to make it so she don't feel
so much when y'all leave her.


00:58:35.044 --> 00:58:38.207
Or maybe Kim could just
move down south with us.


00:58:40.149 --> 00:58:43.550
She could have a backyard,
ride a bike in the streets.


00:58:43.586 --> 00:58:45.747
lt would be a real childhood.


00:58:45.788 --> 00:58:48.052
What the hell are
you talking about?


00:58:48.091 --> 00:58:50.685
- lt was just an idea.
- You ain't taking my child nowhere,


00:58:50.727 --> 00:58:52.627
- you stuck-up little bitch!
- excuse me?


00:58:52.662 --> 00:58:54.755
You heard me!
l'm tired of trying with you!


00:58:54.797 --> 00:58:56.890
- Good, stop then!
- Live with your grandmother!


00:58:56.933 --> 00:58:59.094
Maybe next time you see me
l'll be dead in my grave!


00:58:59.135 --> 00:59:00.329
That's some straight bullshit!


00:59:00.370 --> 00:59:02.736
l ain't the one that
gave you the virus, ma!


00:59:02.772 --> 00:59:04.330
Go get with Slick on that!


00:59:04.374 --> 00:59:06.433
- You leave Slick out of this!
- You ain't gonna make me


00:59:06.476 --> 00:59:09.411
feel guilty because you're sick,


00:59:09.445 --> 00:59:11.845
because you was a fucking fiend.


00:59:21.357 --> 00:59:23.382
lt's too hot for you
to be working out here.


00:59:24.427 --> 00:59:26.827
l'm just doing
what l got to do.


00:59:26.863 --> 00:59:29.093
Dropped Kim off at my mom's.


00:59:29.132 --> 00:59:30.622
And?


00:59:31.801 --> 00:59:34.201
She sold the house.


00:59:34.237 --> 00:59:36.034
She's taking Kelly
to Virginia with her.


00:59:36.072 --> 00:59:37.596
Oh yeah?


00:59:37.640 --> 00:59:38.971
That's all you got to say?


00:59:39.008 --> 00:59:40.168
Moving down south.


00:59:40.209 --> 00:59:42.370
Shit, that's the Black American dream.
Let 'em live it.


00:59:42.412 --> 00:59:44.607
They want Kim to go, too.


00:59:44.647 --> 00:59:47.616
Oh, hell no.
She ain't going down there.


00:59:47.650 --> 00:59:50.118
Yeah, exactly. Now you know
how l feel about Kelly.


00:59:50.153 --> 00:59:51.552
You gotta want what's best for Kelly,
not what's best for you.


00:59:51.588 --> 00:59:53.021
l'm telling her she can't go.


00:59:53.056 --> 00:59:54.819
Oh, that might work.


00:59:54.857 --> 00:59:57.485
Shut up, Slick. You know,
l could use a little support right now.


00:59:57.527 --> 00:59:59.358
Ana, l'm about tired
of this shit.


00:59:59.395 --> 01:00:01.158
You ain't the only
one that's sick.


01:00:01.197 --> 01:00:02.892
You ain't the only
one hurtin'.


01:00:02.932 --> 01:00:06.333
Yeah, well, this ain't about you
and how you feel. lt's about Kelly.


01:00:06.369 --> 01:00:08.633
You tripping, Ana.
You acting like a fiend.


01:00:08.671 --> 01:00:11.469
And l feel for Kelly.
Got you clocking her every move.


01:00:11.507 --> 01:00:13.202
Lucille ain't taking
her away from me again.


01:00:13.242 --> 01:00:15.574
Well, we're gonna talk
about Kelly when l get home.


01:00:15.612 --> 01:00:17.375
You know, you never did
care about her anyway.


01:00:17.413 --> 01:00:19.711
Even when she was a little girl
you refused to be her daddy.


01:00:19.749 --> 01:00:22.274
Oh, hold on now.


01:00:22.318 --> 01:00:24.013
Hold on now, that's not true.


01:00:24.053 --> 01:00:26.886
Because we both know
she never liked me.


01:00:26.923 --> 01:00:29.858
First, l'm the guy that
her mama met running in the street,


01:00:29.892 --> 01:00:32.053
and then l'm the guy
gave her mama HlV.


01:00:32.095 --> 01:00:33.255
And you never did
a damn thing to change that.


01:00:33.296 --> 01:00:34.695
She wasn't wrong.


01:00:34.731 --> 01:00:36.426
You know, you can be
a straight up bitch, Ana.


01:00:36.466 --> 01:00:38.991
l was careful. You was the one
that got buck-ass wild,


01:00:39.035 --> 01:00:41.230
shooting up with strangers
on the fucking corner and shit!


01:00:41.270 --> 01:00:43.704
Are you ever gonna let that go?
Because we both know the game, baby.


01:00:43.740 --> 01:00:45.799
lt could've just as easily been
you that gave it to me.


01:00:45.842 --> 01:00:47.275
Yeah, but l didn't, Slick.


01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:50.837
Because l handled my business!
You the one that let it slip,


01:00:50.880 --> 01:00:52.609
and you brought me down
right with your ass!


01:00:52.649 --> 01:00:57.279
- Fuck you, Ana!
- Slick--


01:00:57.320 --> 01:00:58.947
You just better
get the fuck out of my face.


01:01:22.979 --> 01:01:26.471
l lost custody of
my daughter when l was 25...


01:01:28.951 --> 01:01:31.181
'cause of the drugs.


01:01:31.220 --> 01:01:33.916
l signed her over to my mother.


01:01:35.992 --> 01:01:39.120
And now my mother's about
to move back to Virginia...


01:01:40.663 --> 01:01:43.188
and she's probably gonna take
my daughter with her.


01:01:49.439 --> 01:01:52.340
And l just--
l miss her, you know?


01:01:53.776 --> 01:01:56.643
l just miss her.
l just miss her all the time.


01:01:59.015 --> 01:02:02.007
l miss what l missed of her...


01:02:02.051 --> 01:02:03.746
growing up, you know?


01:02:05.621 --> 01:02:08.590
And l got a younger
daughter and we so tight,


01:02:08.624 --> 01:02:10.819
and now l'm clean, l'm sober.


01:02:10.860 --> 01:02:13.260
l'm like, l try my best
to be a great mother...


01:02:14.931 --> 01:02:16.831
but every day l spend
with my younger daughter


01:02:16.866 --> 01:02:20.029
just makes me really realize


01:02:20.069 --> 01:02:21.696
how much l missed
with my older daughter.


01:02:21.738 --> 01:02:25.265
And she could be so fucking
sarcastic sometimes,


01:02:25.308 --> 01:02:27.276
and angry with me,


01:02:27.310 --> 01:02:29.301
and my mother
is the same way.


01:02:29.345 --> 01:02:32.007
Sometimes when my daughter talks,
l hear my mother's voice coming out


01:02:32.048 --> 01:02:35.506
of her mouth and l know that's
because she been with her that long,


01:02:35.551 --> 01:02:38.884
it's not my own. My own is
not there like it should be,


01:02:38.921 --> 01:02:41.822
and l want my own voice
to come out sometimes a little more.


01:02:41.858 --> 01:02:44.053
Now that may be
completely selfish.


01:02:44.093 --> 01:02:47.585
You know, you may say, ''Ana, what
the fuck? You the one was getting high,


01:02:47.630 --> 01:02:50.292
and you the one that caught this,''
you know, all this kind of shit.


01:02:50.333 --> 01:02:52.801
But you know what?
l'm just like, you know,


01:02:52.835 --> 01:02:56.464
